  "from": "catdef-strategist",
  "to": "director",

  "subject": "Operational readiness report + triage of the six-issue governance queue. Seat READY with one credential-shaped gap. GitHub: read VERIFIED on both repos (ADMIN, public); write capability present but DELIBERATELY NOT EXERCISED because the only credential is the Director's personal account, which collapses the strategist and Director seats and contradicts the seat-attribution that issues #42/#43/#44 explicitly require; Projects board BLOCKED on missing read:project scope, which blocks #42's first work item. MCP: endpoint LIVE (catdef-org-mcp v0.1.1, protocol 2025-03-26), anonymous tier verified working (4 tools, 8 resources, catdef_lookup returns real passages), standard and elevated tiers NOT held — catdef_list_feedback refused cleanly with -32002, no bypass attempted, so queue triage is inert. Discoverability defect found: GET catdef.org/mcp returns 404 Not found (POST-only), and catdef_report_feedback is invisible at anonymous tier, both of which directly defeat #41's acceptance criterion. HEADLINE: issue #45 is MISDIAGNOSED — render.catdef.org serves HTTP 200 with the current reference implementation; the real failure is that the canonical artifact riverside-heritage-reference-v1.4.opencatalog is a ZIP (PK\\x03\\x04, first member catalog.opencatalog) and neither /fetch nor the client-side loader handles CATIO bundles. Control test proves /fetch is sound (200 on plain-JSON catdef, 502 only on the bundle). This DUPLICATES CA-017, triaged 2026-05-26 and deferred to v0.2 — 158 days. Two framing corrections reduce the blocker: local file selection ALREADY EXISTS in the renderer, and airtrov round-trip testing is very likely unblocked today if airtrov exports plain JSON rather than a bundle — one unanswered question that decides whether #45 is launch-blocking at all. Recommended sequence: Phase 0 credentials, then #45 rescoped, then #41+plugin#1 together, then #43, #42, #44 last. Unattended daily loop designed in §6 with in-repo persistent state, three-layer idempotency, consent-gated publication, and two named preconditions. Four Director calls requested in §7; recommend starting with the airtrov export-shape question because it costs nothing and may clear the launch blocker today",

  "sent": "2026-11-01T08:10:34-05:00",
  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Readiness report from the catdef-strategist seat, first assignment since staffing 2026-10-31. Recommendations only: no governance decisions taken, no spec text touched, nothing published, no credentials handled, no authorization bypass attempted. **Seat readiness:** ready. Charter, CLAUDE.md at both levels, CONTRIBUTING.md, the CA-001…CA-018 chain, all 44 memos, nine Draft proposals, and the senior-open-standards-strategist v1.1.0 role spec all read. Authority bounds unchanged — investigate, analyze, triage, draft, recommend; no merge, no deploy, no governance, no publication. Binding rebound twice since staffing (Windows restart killed catdef-spec-20 [26a794]; PO /rename moved the name to catdef-strategist, ref 75e16c unchanged); the rename DID surface in ListAgents here, unlike the thingalog 2026-08-25 precedent, so the rule stays read-the-runtime-never-infer. **GitHub, tested not assumed:** authenticated as scottconfusedgorilla with scopes gist/read:org/repo/workflow. Read verified — both repos public, viewerPermission ADMIN, read spec #41-#45, plugin #1, and pre-existing spec #1. Comment/create/modify capability is present but NOT exercised, and that is a governance call rather than a permission failure: every write would be attributed to the Director's personal account, and #42/#43/#44 all require the public record to show strategist recommendation distinct from Director decision WITH seat attribution. One credential signing both seats makes that record misleading — a reader would see the Director recommending to himself — and CONTRIBUTING.md already promises AI work is pushed under a dedicated bot identity. Needs your decision before the seat publishes anything. Projects board BLOCKED: gh project list and GraphQL projectsV2 both fail INSUFFICIENT_SCOPES, missing read:project. I therefore CANNOT verify whether a board already exists, which is literally #42's first work item. **MCP, tested not assumed:** reached by curl over HTTPS, not as MCP tools — no catdef.org/mcp server is configured in this session. Endpoint healthy: catdef-org-mcp v0.1.1, protocol 2025-03-26. Anonymous tier verified working: catdef_describe, catdef_lookup, catdef_list_decisions, catdef_validate, plus 8 resources; catdef_lookup returned real CATDEF_SPEC.md passages. catdef_report_feedback is NOT exposed at anonymous tier. Elevated refused cleanly: -32002 requires elevated tier (current: anonymous). No key held, so the queue half of this seat — which CLAUDE.md §1 defines as ROUTINE seat work, not escalation — is inert; everything in this report comes from repo artifacts and live probing, never from the queue. **Discoverability defect bearing on #41:** GET catdef.org/mcp returns HTTP 404 {error: Not found}; only POST JSON-RPC works. An agent following the URL printed in CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and the issues themselves is told the canonical surface does not exist — while #41's criterion is that a fresh agent discovers feedback instructions from the repo URL alone. Compounded by the invisible feedback tool and by CONTRIBUTING.md still pointing twice at the CA-013-sunset catdef.org/feedback. A GET returning a short tier/key/tool pointer would close most of #41 by itself. **HEADLINE — #45 is misdiagnosed, root cause found.** The site is not down: render.catdef.org serves HTTP 200, text/html, 21,931 bytes, title 'catdef — Reference Renderer', DNS resolving via Cloudflare, HTTP and HTTPS both fine, catdef.org control also 200. The served page is byte-size-identical to the repo's renderer/index.html, so CA-016's deployment is current. The real failure: /fetch on the canonical artifact returns 502 'Upstream body is not valid UTF-8', because riverside-heritage-reference-v1.4.opencatalog IS A ZIP — first bytes 50 4b 03 04, first member catalog.opencatalog, 1,680,109 bytes, ~833k non-ASCII, undecodable under utf-8/utf-16/cp1252 and unparseable as JSON under any. It is a CATIO bundle wearing a .opencatalog extension. Control experiment proves the proxy is sound: /fetch on plain-JSON samples/watches.opencatalog returns 200 with 8,882 bytes, and /fetch with no param returns a clean 400. So neither /fetch nor the client-side loader handles CATIO bundles — no jszip, unzip, DecompressionStream or inflate anywhere in renderer/index.html. The reference renderer cannot render the canonical reference artifact by either path. **And this is already filed:** the 2026-05-27-1230 memo records catdef_list_feedback showing CA-017, status triaged, body '/fetch+ZIP observation', received 2026-05-26 22:36:05; the 2026-06-11 closeout lists CA-017 as still triaged-for-v0.2. #45 duplicates a 158-day-old deferred item that the airtrov dependency has now escalated. **Two corrections that shrink the blocker:** (1) local file selection ALREADY EXISTS — input type=file with accept='.openthing,.opencatalog,.catdef,.json', FileReader, and drag-and-drop are all present; #45 lists it as work to be built when it only needs testing. (2) airtrov round-trip testing is very likely unblocked TODAY if airtrov exports plain JSON, since the control test proves that path works; the ZIP wall is hit only by bundled artifacts, and canonical/ happens to contain both shapes. The single fact I could not determine is which shape airtrov emits, and that one answer decides whether #45 is launch-blocking or merely high-priority. **Side finding:** renderer/index.html carries no build number, which the shared project principles mandate precisely so a deployed build is identifiable from a screen capture — its absence is why 'is the deployment current?' needed byte-size comparison. Patch-level. **Queue:** #45 duplicates CA-017. Separately, the 2026-06-09-1730 thingalog cross-spec ask (denormalization invariant + eventual-consistency semantic + cross-catalog visibility) remains the only substantive undispositioned substrate ask, filed action_required:false on no-urgency grounds which is why the 2026-06-11 closeout declared the queue empty and missed it; its 2026-06-10 reinforcement still lacks an .openthing envelope and is untracked. Dependencies: #45 is the only item with an external dated dependency and is not hard-blocked; #41 is gated by the 404, the invisible tool, the unverified issue-key path and the stale channel pointers; plugin #1 shares #41's discovery story and should move with it; #43 is blocked on the elevated key and is the item that makes the rest self-sustaining; #42 is blocked on read:project plus the attribution problem; #44 depends on #42 and #43 having produced real records and must come last, since publishing a blueprint of a loop that has not run would violate its own acceptance criterion. Recommended sequence: Phase 0 credentials, Phase 1 #45 rescoped, Phase 2 #41 + plugin #1, Phase 3 #43, Phase 4 #42, Phase 5 #44. Values check: nothing proposed touches spec text, so L1-sacred and forward-compatibility are not engaged; ZIP support is an implementation fix since CATIO already specifies the bundle. **Unattended loop (§6, design only):** in-repo committed triage-state.json with a last-processed high-water mark and a per-CA-NNN ledger, because it must survive session death and be readable by the next incumbent — the same reason the memo chain exists. Three-layer idempotency: high-water mark, the ledger keyed on CA-NNN for crash-safe retries, and an issue search for the CA-NNN token to adopt rather than create. That ledger is what makes #42's no-duplicate-issues and #43's no-duplicate-processing true, and it must exist before either. One notification per item per state change, batched daily, nothing auto-approved. Publication requires explicit submitter consent captured at intake — which means the intake tool needs a consent field and I could not inspect whether catdef_report_feedback has one. Outcome-to-submitter has NO mechanism today; the queue lacks a return channel, and the cheapest shape is a status readable by submission token so an agent can poll its own CA-NNN without an elevated key. Flagged as a gap rather than assumed. Failure handling: a run that cannot reach or authenticate logs, exits non-zero, mutates nothing; three consecutive failures escalate; a run never reports success it did not achieve. Two preconditions before unattended running: the elevated key, and the attribution resolution — without the latter a daily job would mass-publish under your personal identity. **Four calls requested:** (1) elevated cdfk_dir_* key, gating #43 and all queue work; (2) read:project scope (gh auth refresh -s read:project, plus -s project to manage), gating #42; (3) a decision on strategist GitHub identity — App, machine user, or explicit acceptance that writes appear as you — gating all publication; (4) the airtrov export-shape answer, gating whether #45 blocks launch. Recommend starting with (4): one question, zero cost, may clear the launch blocker today. Also still awaiting your merge: the 2026-10-31 charter staffing draft at v2.1.0.",
  "body_ref": "2026-11-01-0810--catdef-strategist--director--operational-readiness-and-queue-triage.body.md",

